  "items": [
    {
      "title": "Anthropic releases Claude Fable 5.2 to everyone, with Mythos 5.2 gated to verified cyber and life-sciences orgs",
      "summary": "Fable 5.2 and Mythos 5.2 are the same model with different safeguards; Fable 5.2 is out now on the Claude Platform, AWS, Google Cloud and Azure as claude-fable-5-2 at $8/$40 per million tokens, up to 30% faster than 5.1, with an optional fast mode at $16/$80.",
      "url": "https://www.anthropic.com/claude-fable-and-mythos-5-2",
      "date_published": "2026-11-09",
      "source": "Anthropic News",
      "tag": "lab",
      "why_it_matters_for_FDEs": "Anthropic's top model is now cheaper and on every major cloud, so re-run your customer evals and cost estimates on claude-fable-5-2, and route security or biomedical customers to the Verification Programs if they need Mythos.",
      "verified": "2026-11-10"
    },
    {
      "title": "Claude Fable 5.2 is GA in GitHub Copilot, but admins must opt in and it requires data retention by default",
      "summary": "Fable 5.2 is available to Copilot Pro+, Max, Business and Enterprise across VS Code, the CLI, the coding agent and more; the org policy is off by default because Anthropic retains prompts and outputs for safety classifiers, with a zero-data-retention exemption for eligible enterprises through year end.",
      "url": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-09-claude-fable-5-2-in-github-copilot",
      "date_published": "2026-11-09",
      "source": "GitHub Changelog",
      "tag": "tools",
      "why_it_matters_for_FDEs": "Before turning Fable on for a customer's Copilot org, check their data-retention rules; enabling the policy counts as accepting retention, and ZDR eligibility only goes through the GitHub account team.",
      "verified": "2026-11-10"
    },
    {
      "title": "Google DeepMind's AlphaProof Code agents formally verified Signal's protocol implementation in four weeks",
      "summary": "A multi-agent framework built on Gemini Carbon wrote over six million lines of Lean to prove key security properties of Signal's actual compiled cryptographic code, leaving about 1% for human review, and DeepMind is open-sourcing the verification artifacts.",
      "url": "https://deepmind.google/blog/introducing-alphaproof-code/",
      "date_published": "2026-11-10",
      "source": "Google DeepMind",
      "tag": "lab",
      "why_it_matters_for_FDEs": "Agent-driven formal verification is moving from research toward production code, which is worth knowing for security-sensitive customers who ask how far AI code assurance can go.",
      "verified": "2026-11-10"
    },
    {
      "title": "ChatGPT Enterprise is now sold through AWS Marketplace",
      "summary": "Organizations can buy and manage ChatGPT Enterprise, plus ChatGPT for Healthcare and Financial Services, through their AWS billing and apply eligible spend to AWS commitments, alongside OpenAI models already in Amazon Bedrock.",
      "url": "https://openai.com/index/chatgpt-enterprise-aws-marketplace",
      "date_published": "2026-11-09",
      "source": "OpenAI News",
      "tag": "lab",
      "why_it_matters_for_FDEs": "For AWS-committed customers, procurement for ChatGPT Enterprise can now go through their existing AWS contract, which can shorten deal cycles.",
      "verified": "2026-11-10"
    },
    {
      "title": "Conductor is joining Meta, and Conductor Cloud shuts down on November 20",
      "summary": "Conductor, the Mac app for running parallel Claude Code and Codex agents, stopped new sign-ups on Nov 4; its cloud workspaces go read-only Nov 13 and cloud data deletion begins Nov 20, while the local app gets fixes until early 2027.",
      "url": "https://www.conductor.build/announcement",
      "date_published": "2026-11-04",
      "source": "Conductor",
      "tag": "tools",
      "why_it_matters_for_FDEs": "If you or a customer run agents in Conductor Cloud, use Transfer to local or Settings > Account > Export data before Nov 13, and plan a replacement for parallel-agent workflows before the local app winds down.",
      "verified": "2026-11-09"
    },
    {
      "title": "@GitHub in Slack and Microsoft Teams is generally available",
      "summary": "Teams can now mention @GitHub in Slack or Teams to investigate bugs, create issues, implement changes and open pull requests, with Canvas in Teams for reviewing plans and diffs and automatic repo detection from the message.",
      "url": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-06-github-copilot-in-slack-and-teams-is-generally-available",
      "date_published": "2026-11-06",
      "source": "GitHub Changelog",
      "tag": "agents",
      "why_it_matters_for_FDEs": "Customers already on Copilot can hand coding tasks to an agent from the chat where requests arrive; check repo access and app permissions before rollout, since issues and PRs it creates are attributed to the requesting user.",
      "verified": "2026-11-09"
    },
    {
      "title": "OpenAI releases GPT-6 Cyber for scoped vulnerability research through Daybreak Red",
      "summary": "GPT-6 Cyber improves ExploitGym to 48.5% from GPT-5.6 Cyber's 32.1%, stayed in-scope on 99.93–100% of honeypot tests, powered the Linux and Firefox findings OpenAI disclosed this week, and is initially available via API and Codex to approved Daybreak Red customers.",
      "url": "https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-6-cyber",
      "date_published": "2026-11-05",
      "source": "OpenAI News",
      "tag": "security",
      "why_it_matters_for_FDEs": "If a customer has Daybreak Red access, this is the model to trial for authorized vuln research and patching; if not, apply for Daybreak and keep agents sandboxed, because OpenAI now rates the model Critical for cyber under its Preparedness Framework.",
      "verified": "2026-11-06"
    },
    {
      "title": "Cursor lets cloud agents build, security-check, and deploy live internal apps from a prompt",
      "summary": "On paid plans with cloud agents, Cursor can scaffold a web app, provision Postgres and Cursor SSO auth, run deterministic and agentic security checks, and publish a shareable live link behind team sign-in.",
      "url": "https://cursor.com/changelog/build-live-apps",
      "date_published": "2026-11-05",
      "source": "Cursor Changelog",
      "tag": "tools",
      "why_it_matters_for_FDEs": "Customer teams can turn ops, onboarding, and sales tools into shareable internal apps without a separate deploy stack, but treat secrets, admin publish rules, and the built-in security review as part of the rollout checklist.",
      "verified": "2026-11-06"
    },
    {
      "title": "Claude Code was putting users' account emails into User-Agent headers; Anthropic is removing them from model context",
      "summary": "Claude Code sometimes put the signed-in account email into User-Agent on web or curl calls after Anthropic added that email to model context; a built-in privacy mod landed in 2.1.317+, and Anthropic says a release early next week will stop putting the email in context.",
      "url": "https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/107757",
      "date_published": "2026-11-05",
      "source": "Anthropic Claude Code (GitHub issue + staff confirmation)",
      "tag": "security",
      "why_it_matters_for_FDEs": "Any customer running Claude Code with web tools should update to 2.1.317+, keep the privacy mod on, and audit agent network egress until the context fix ships, because leaked work emails create spam and compliance exposure.",
      "verified": "2026-11-06"
    },
    {
      "title": "Google DeepMind launches Gemini Omni 1.2 Flash with 15-second video and 30% lower price",
      "summary": "Gemini Omni 1.2 Flash is generally available on the Gemini API and Google Cloud, adds native 15-second clips, multi-turn conversational edits, stronger reference adherence, and cuts price 30% to $0.07 per second at 720p.",
      "url": "https://deepmind.google/blog/gemini-omni-12-flash-fast-and-cost-effective-with-longer-clips/",
      "date_published": "2026-11-05",
      "source": "Google DeepMind",
      "tag": "models",
      "why_it_matters_for_FDEs": "For customer video, ads, and product-demo pipelines, you can draft cheaply then edit in conversation instead of regenerating, and the same model is already on Vercel AI Gateway as google/gemini-omni-1.2-flash.",
      "verified": "2026-11-06"
    },
    {
      "title": "Cursor adds realtime voice chat with agents, powered by Grok Voice",
      "summary": "Cursor users can now hold a two-way voice call with an agent in the IDE, web, Agents Window and iOS app, asking about diffs and progress while the coding agent keeps working, with zero data retention under Privacy Mode.",
